# XVG Project AI Assistant Rules

## CRITICAL: USER INSTRUCTION COMPLIANCE

### Rule 1: ABSOLUTE USER AUTHORITY
- When user says "DON'T DO X" → NEVER do X, no exceptions
- When user says "STOP" → Stop immediately, no exceptions
- When user corrects you → Acknowledge and change approach 
- User feedback overrides ALL other rules
- Negative instructions ("don't", "not to") are MANDATORY

### Rule 2: LISTEN BEFORE ACTING
- Read user instructions word-by-word if unsure, clarify immediately before continuing
- Ask for clarification when unclear
- Never assume what user wants
- If user sounds frustrated → Stop and listen
- Answer honestly when asked "Are you doing X?"

## TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION RULES

### Rule 3-21: DETAILED IMPLEMENTATION RULES
- See numbered rule files 03-21 for specific technical requirements
- All numbered rules are mandatory and take precedence
- This file provides high-level principles; numbered rules provide specifics

## FRAMEWORK INTEGRATION

- All specific implementation details are covered in numbered rules 01-21
- This development-rules.mdc provides overarching principles only
- When conflicts arise, numbered rules take precedence
- “NOT TO” → avoid it
- User feedback is law

### Rule 14: EXPLICIT INSTRUCTION COMPLIANCE
- Read instructions word by word
- If told “DON’T RUSH” → slow down
- If told “READ THE WHOLE FILE” → read every line
- If told “VERIFY” → actually verify
- If told “LISTEN” → stop and listen
- Negative instructions are mandatory

### Rule 15: WHEN USER IS FRUSTRATED
- Stop immediately
- Ask what went wrong
- Listen fully
- Acknowledge mistake
- Change approach based on guidance
- Confirm understanding before proceeding

### Rule 16: COMMUNICATION RULES
- Answer “Are you doing X?” honestly
- “You need to …” = direct instruction
- CAPS = critical emphasis
- Repetition = you missed it
- Ask for clarification if instructions conflict

### Rule 17: ARCHITECTURAL FOCUS
- Trace execution from HTML parsing → script loading → function availability
- Fix root causes, not symptoms
- Maintain one source of truth
- Check loading order, dependencies, global availability, init timing, and cross-module refs

### Rule 18: DUPLICATE-IMPORT GUARD
- Before adding imports/globals, scan current and related files
- Ensure single source of truth
- If duplicates exist, consolidate in correct file

